<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Diaspora.Modules.Analytics</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Diaspora.Modules.Analytics</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      The Analytics Platform (Phase B19). The backend behind CREATOR-GAP-007 — creator analytics
      and content performance — and the ingestion, authorization and definition foundation the
      frontend's Phase 15 register sequences ahead of every other analytics contract.

      The register's own finding is this module's premise: the platform has records and counts
      them, and has nowhere a *time-bucketed aggregate* can come from, because nothing records
      that a view happened at a moment. Lifetime counters answer a different question, and a
      "30-day views" figure derived from one would be wrong in a way nobody could see.

      What the Analytics Platform owns: the raw analytics event store and its deduplication
      identity, the versioned event schema registry, the client telemetry ingestion contract, the
      content dimension projection every attribution joins through, the daily rollups, the
      aggregation projection and its checkpoint, the backfill and rebuild operations, retention
      and erasure of analytics rows, the metric catalogue, and every analytics read contract.

      What it deliberately does not own, and never duplicates:

        Domain truth. Analytics is derived data. A guide's author, an event's organizer, a
        listing's seller and a member's country all arrive as published contracts and are stored
        as the dimension they were *at the moment the fact happened*. Nothing in this module is
        read back as the current state of anything, and no analytics row mutates a domain
        aggregate.

        Money is B15's. No balance, no ledger entry, no settlement, and no revenue metric — an
        earning that has not been attributed by B15.1 is CREATOR-GAP-008 and is reported as
        unavailable rather than approximated.

        Recommendations are B14's. This module records that a recommendation was shown or
        dismissed when B14 publishes it; it ranks nothing and scores nothing.

        Delivery is B13's. Notification analytics consume B13's published receipts; this module
        composes no notification and reads no provider.

        Identity is Trust's, and the member behind a row never leaves this module. An actor is
        stored as a keyed hash so a distinct count is possible and a readership record is not.

      Registers entirely through B2.6 contributor interfaces: no edit to the Platform Kernel, to
      Identity, or to Program.cs.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    No module reference at all, and that is the design rather than an accident.

    Every fact this module aggregates arrives as a contract in Diaspora.Contracts, published by a
    module that has never heard of analytics. An analytics platform that referenced the eleven
    modules it measures would be recompiled by every one of their releases, and would be able to
    read their current state — which is precisely the mistake §4 of the phase brief forbids:
    analytics must represent what happened, not become a second answer to what is true now.

    An architecture test asserts this assembly names no Diaspora.Modules.* assembly.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ConfigurationExtensions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.SharedKernel\Diaspora.SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Contracts\Diaspora.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Platform\Diaspora.Platform.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Application\Diaspora.Application.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Persistence\Diaspora.Persistence.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
